// =========================================================================
// niri autostart - what hypr/autostart.lua starts, started by niri
// =========================================================================
//
// Include this from ~/.config/niri/config.kdl:
//
//     include "~/Work/fd44_hyprdot/niri/autostart.kdl"
//
// MOST OF THIS IS COMPOSITOR-NEUTRAL ALREADY. These are the same scripts
// hypr/autostart.lua runs; they talk to quickshell, systemd and the filesystem
// rather than to a compositor, so they need no niri versions.
//
// PATHS ARE SPELLED OUT, unlike the Hyprland side. That file reaches the
// repository as "$HOME/.config/hypr/../bin/...", which works because
// ~/.config/hypr is a symlink into the checkout. ~/.config/niri is not a
// symlink - it is a real file with include lines - so there is no such
// shortcut and the location is written once, here.
//
// ORDER MATTERS IN ONE PLACE: icon-bridge.sh before `qs -d`, because the bridge
// is what lets quickshell see the icon theme at all, and a bar started before it
// draws empty boxes until the next restart.

spawn-at-startup "sh" "-c" "$HOME/Work/fd44_hyprdot/bin/icon-bridge.sh >/dev/null 2>&1; qs -d"

// The wallpaper quickshell draws, restored from what was set last, then its
// thumbnails rebuilt in the background for the picker.
spawn-at-startup "sh" "-c" "$HOME/Work/fd44_hyprdot/bin/wallpaper.sh restore"
spawn-at-startup "sh" "-c" "$HOME/Work/fd44_hyprdot/bin/wallpaper.sh thumbs"

// The palette. KNOWN GAP: theme.sh is one of the scripts that calls hyprctl, so
// parts of it will fail under niri until that is ported. It is left in rather
// than dropped, because the parts that set GTK, kitty and quickshell colours do
// not involve the compositor and are most of what it does.
spawn-at-startup "sh" "-c" "$HOME/Work/fd44_hyprdot/bin/theme.sh restore"

// The lock screen at login, for an autologin session. hyprlock speaks
// ext-session-lock-v1, which niri implements, so this carries over unchanged.
spawn-at-startup "sh" "-c" "$HOME/Work/fd44_hyprdot/bin/lock-at-login.sh"

// Audio interface gain, which is a USB device setting and has nothing to do with
// the compositor.
spawn-at-startup "sh" "-c" "$HOME/Work/fd44_hyprdot/bin/evo4-gain.sh"

// THE WORKING TERMINAL, on workspace 1 and full width.
//
// --app-id kitty-framework is what niri/rules.kdl matches on, and it has to be
// a name of its own: a rule keyed on plain "kitty" would pin every terminal
// opened with Mod+Return to workspace 1 at full width.
//
// `tmux new-session -A` attaches to "framework" if it exists and creates it
// otherwise, so this is safe to run again after the compositor restarts - it
// finds the session that survived rather than starting a second one. The
// command after it only runs when the session is NEW; attaching ignores it,
// which is the behaviour wanted here.
//
// claude --resume takes a conversation id. Resuming the SAME id at every login
// means every session continues one long conversation; starting a fresh one is
// `claude` with no arguments. Two instances resuming one id at once is worth
// avoiding - this one is attached to a tmux session, so a second login finds
// the first rather than racing it.
spawn-at-startup "sh" "-c" "kitty --app-id kitty-framework -e tmux new-session -A -s framework claude --resume 4c3c50be-ace6-48fa-a669-28809a94ba06"

// THE SYSTEMD USER SERVICES ARE MOSTLY LEFT TO niri-session, which binds
// graphical-session.target the way uwsm does on the Hyprland side, so anything
// ENABLED for the user starts with the session and starting it again here would
// be a second copy or a no-op. pipewire and wireplumber come up that way.
//
// EXCEPT hypridle, AND THE REASON IS WRITTEN DOWN IN hypr/autostart.lua ALREADY:
// nixpkgs ships hypridle.service with `preset: ignored`, so it is never enabled
// and niri-session has nothing to start. The Hyprland side hit this on the
// gaming desktop on 2026-09-24 - the unit sat "inactive (dead)" with no journal
// entries and the screen never locked - and fixed it with the guarded fallback
// below. This file assumed niri-session covered it and so did not carry the
// fix, which is why framework00 woke from sleep unlocked: nothing was running
// to answer logind's Lock signal.
//
// SAME GUARD, SAME ORDER. If the unit IS enabled somewhere, systemd owns it and
// this does nothing; if a hypridle is already running, this does nothing; only
// otherwise does it start one. hypridle is not a binary nixpkgs wraps, so its
// comm is plain `hypridle` and one spelling is enough.
spawn-at-startup "sh" "-c" "systemctl --user -q is-enabled hypridle.service 2>/dev/null || pgrep -x hypridle >/dev/null 2>&1 || hypridle &"
